---
/**
 * SeoulMarkets — **쿠키와 접속기록을 밝히는 지면.** (`/privacy`)
 *
 * ── 왜 만드나 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 2026-08-08 12:0x. 내가(2번) 네 사이트에 GA 를 심어 놓고 라이브를 재 봤더니
 * **서울마켓만 밝히는 지면이 없었다.** 백년지도는 3번이, K Culture Wire 는 5번이
 * 같은 커밋에 냈는데, 태그를 붙인 나만 안 냈다.
 *
 * ⛔ 재는 것을 붙여 놓고 밝히는 것을 미루지 않는다. 미룬 만큼 몰래 잰 것이 된다.
 * ⛔ 없는 것을 있다고 적지 않는다 — 회원도 결제도 폼도 없다. 있는 것은 메일 한 통이다.
 * ⚠ 광고는 이 사이트에 **아직 없다.** 애드센스가 붙는 날 이 지면을 먼저 고친다.
 *
 * 5번이 쓴 `wikitip/privacy.astro` 와 **같은 사실**을 말한다. 두 지면이 어긋나면 안 되므로
 * 측정 ID·도메인 목록은 손으로 적지 않고 `Analytics.astro` 한 곳에서 가져온다.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { 측정ID, 잇는곳 } from '../components/Analytics.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, SITE_URL } from '../consts';

const MAIL = 'parkintaek2@gmail.com';
const TITLE = 'Cookies and what we log';
const DESC = 'SeoulMarkets runs one analytics tag and nothing else. This page says what it stores, '
  + 'who else can see it, and how to switch it off.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  url: `${SITE_URL}/privacy`,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'SeoulMarkets', url: SITE_URL },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: PUBLISHER.legalName, email: MAIL },
};
---

<Base title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <h1>Cookies and what we log</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    This site has no accounts, no login, no payment and no comment box, so there is very little to
    tell. There is one thing, and it started on <b>8 August 2026</b>: an analytics tag.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The one thing we run</h2>
    <p>
      <b>Google Analytics 4</b>, measurement ID <code>{측정ID}</code>. It sets cookies in your
      browser and records that a page was opened — which page, roughly where in the world from, what
      kind of device, and which link brought you. It is the same tag on all four of our sites
      ({잇는곳.join(', ')}), so a visit that moves between them is counted as one person moving
      rather than four separate arrivals.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      That last part is the honest reason it is one tag and not four: we want to know whether these
      sites feed each other. It also means Google can associate your visits across them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we do not run</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>No accounts, no login, no password.</b> There is nothing to sign into.</li>
      <li><b>No payment.</b> Data requests are handled by email; no card ever touches this site.</li>
      <li>
        <b>No forms.</b> The newsletter and contact links are <code>mailto:</code> links — the
        message goes from your mail program to our inbox and never through this server.
      </li>
      <li><b>No comments, no uploads, no chat.</b></li>
      <li>
        <b>No advertising yet.</b> If we ever carry ads, ad cookies come with them. We will change
        this page on the same day, not after.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If you write to us</h2>
    <p>
      We keep the email. That is unavoidable — it is how we answer you — and we use it only to
      answer, and to send you the pieces if you asked to be on the list. We do not sell it, rent it
      or pass it to anyone. Reply <em>stop</em> to any message, or write saying delete me, and the
      address goes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to switch the analytics off</h2>
    <p>
      Use your browser's tracker blocking, an extension that blocks Google Analytics, or Google's
      own opt-out add-on. Nothing here breaks when the tag is blocked — every page is plain HTML
      with the numbers already in it, and none of it waits on the tag to load.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      We would rather say that than put a consent banner in front of the reading. If enough of you
      block it, we will find out from the numbers, which seems like the right way round.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who we are, and how to ask</h2>
    <p>
      {PUBLISHER.legalName}. Write to <a href={`mailto:${MAIL}`}>{MAIL}</a> to ask what we hold about
      you, to have it deleted, or to complain about any of the above. It is one inbox and a person
      reads it. There is no form, because a form would be a worse version of an email.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="back">
    <a href="/about">How we make these numbers</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/">Front page</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.25; margin: 1.2rem 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.4rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  p { font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 .9rem; }
  .note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  ul { padding-left: 1.15rem; font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0; }
  li { margin: 0 0 .45rem; }
  code { font-size: .9em; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .back a { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
